{
  "source": "SHA-256 is defined in NIST FIPS 180-4. This lesson models Semaphore's identity commitments, Merkle group roots, and (external) nullifier hashing using domain-separated SHA-256 plus an explicit length-prefix encoding for strings/bytes. Merkle hashing uses 0x00 for leaf domain and 0x01 for internal node domain with a deterministic duplicate-last rule for odd node counts. Expected values were computed from this repository's reference implementation (phases/13-zk-engineering/11-semaphore/code/main.py) to lock behavior.",
